The  system  defines  a set of signals that may be delivered to a
process.  Signal delivery resembles the occurrence of a  hardware
interrupt:  the  signal  is  normally blocked from further occur‐
rence, the current process context is saved, and  a  new  one  is
built.   A  process may specify a to which a signal is delivered,
