That is to say, the behaviour of such functions when called  from
a  signal  handler  is undefined.  In general though, signal han‐
dlers should do little more than set a flag; most  other  actions
are  not  safe.   Also, it is good practice to make a copy of the
global variable and restore it before returning from  the  signal
handler.   This  protects against the side effect of being set by
functions called from inside the signal handler.  There are three
